// smp_initiator.nv — the Security Manager as the
// initiating device.
//
// The Central is the initiating device of a pairing ([Vol 3] Part H,
// Section 2.4.1): it sends the Pairing Request, or starts the pairing a
// Peripheral's Security Request asks for (Section 2.4.6), runs the
// association model the Pairing Feature Exchange selects as the
// initiator (Sections 2.3.5.5 and 2.3.5.6), starts the encryption of
// the link with the key that came out of it (Section 2.4.4), and
// distributes the keys its Initiator Key Distribution field promised
// (Section 3.6.1).  smp_responder.nv is the Peripheral's half of
// the same procedures.
//
// The two halves share what is direction-neutral: the commands and their
// field values (smp.nv), the crypto and the key formats (smp_keys.nv),
// the bond record and the security level it gives (smp_bond.nv), the
// phases, the verdicts of the checks on a received command, the
// configuration, the state of a pairing, the procedures both ends run the
// same way and the association-model tables with the AuthReq they build
// and the LE security mode 1 levels that come out of them (smp_core.nv),
// which take both devices' parameters and therefore read the same from
// either side.
//
// The procedure is one pure function, shaped exactly like the
// responder's:
//
//   let step = smp_initiator.handle(state, input, now_ms)
//   state = step.state
//   for pdu in step.pdus           // SMP commands for L2CAP CID 0x0006
//       send_on_smp_channel(pdu)
//   match step.action               // at most one
//       StartEncryption(ltk, ediv, rand)   // LE Start Encryption
//       ...
//
// It performs no I/O and holds no clock: the program passes the time in
// milliseconds with every input and sends `Tick` while a procedure runs,
// so the same code runs on a PC and on a board.
//
// LE Secure Connections works the way the responder's does, which is the
// way a conforming Central does it: after the Pairing Response the
// initiator sends its Pairing Public Key, the responder answers with its
// own public key and its Pairing Confirm, and the initiator then sends Na
// and, once Nb is in, its DHKey Check.  There is no Pairing Confirm from
// the initiator in Just Works and Numeric Comparison; Passkey Entry sends
// one per round and Out of Band sends none (Sections 2.3.5.6.2 to
// 2.3.5.6.4).
//
// Choices this module makes where the specification leaves them open:
//   * a Security Request that arrives while a pairing runs is ignored
//     (Section 2.4.6 forbids sending one then);
//   * a Pairing Request, which only the initiating device sends, is
//     answered with Pairing Failed (Pdu Not Supported) and a command
//     the procedure does not expect at that point with Unspecified
//     Reason, as the responder answers a Security Request;
//   * a Pairing Response whose IO Capability, OOB data flag or Maximum
//     Encryption Key Size this device cannot pair under answers Pairing
//     Failed with the same reason the responder would use for a Pairing
//     Request it cannot take (Sections 2.3.5.1 and 2.3.4); a responder
//     that answers without the SC bit this device asked for pairs in LE
//     legacy, and only a device that requires them (Secure Connections
//     Only mode, or LE security mode 1 level 4) answers Authentication
//     Requirements (Section 2.3.5.6);
//   * a peer that is already bonded is encrypted with, not paired again:
//     `StartPairing` and a Security Request start the encryption
//     procedure with the bond's LTK in place of the Pairing Request
//     (Section 2.4.4.2);
//   * the LTK this device uses to encrypt is the Peripheral's for LE
//     legacy pairing and the f5 key of the pairing for LE Secure
//     Connections, with EDIV and Rand zero (Section 2.4.4.1);
//   * a bond this device holds reads the same in either role: `ltk`,
//     `ediv` and `rand` are the key it encrypts with as the Central, and
//     `peer_ltk`, `peer_ediv` and `peer_rand` the key it distributed and
//     would be asked for as the Peripheral (Section 2.4.5.1).
//
// Not done here: cross-transport key derivation (LinkKey, Section
// 2.3.5.7) is outside an LE-only Host, and the LinkKey bit is answered
// as zero.

use smp
use smp.{ Command, Reason }
use smp_core
use smp_core.{ Role, Phase, Method, SmpConfig }
use smp_keys
use smp_keys.{ PublicKey, KeyPair }
use smp_bond

// ── Inputs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Connected starts a connection: the addresses the Controller reported in
// the LE Connection Complete event (own and peer, type 0 public or 1
// random, least significant octet first) and the bond the program found
// for the peer (`SmpBondStore.find`), if any.  Disconnected ends it.
// Pdu is an SMP command received on CID 0x0006, which includes the
// Peripheral's Security Request.  StartPairing is the BTP Pair command
// and the answer to that request: it sends the Pairing Request, or
// starts the encryption procedure when the peer is bonded.  Tick lets
// the timer run.  EncryptionChanged is the Encryption Change or
// Encryption Key Refresh Complete event (Sections 7.7.8 and 7.7.39).
// PasskeyEntered answers RequestPasskey (a negative value: the user
// cancelled) and NumericConfirmed answers ConfirmNumericValue.
// DhKeyComputed answers `dhkey_request` (empty: the computation failed).
// SendKeypress sends a Keypress Notification while the user types the
// passkey.  SetLegacyOobTk and SetPeerOobData hold the out of band data
// received from the peer: the TK of LE legacy pairing, or r and C of LE
// Secure Connections (empty lists remove them).  CreateOobData makes the
// local r and C to send out of band, and SetLocalOobData holds an r the
// device published before it was this half's to make: the BTP commands
// that carry out of band data run before the Connect whose role decides
// which half pairs, so the session hands the published r to the half the
// connection's role names.  Reseed mixes 16 octets into the random number
// generator.  Cancel aborts a pairing in progress.
pub enum SmpInitInput
    Connected(own_address_type: Int, own_address: [u8], peer_address_type: Int, peer_address: [u8],
              bond: ?SmpBond)
    Disconnected
    Pdu(pdu: [u8])
    StartPairing(level: Int)
    Tick
    EncryptionChanged(enabled: Bool)
    PasskeyEntered(passkey: Int)
    NumericConfirmed(accepted: Bool)
    DhKeyComputed(dhkey: [u8])
    SendKeypress(notification_type: Int)
    SetLegacyOobTk(tk: [u8])
    SetPeerOobData(r: [u8], c: [u8])
    CreateOobData
    SetLocalOobData(r: [u8])
    Reseed(seed: [u8])
    Cancel

// ── Actions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// DisplayPasskey: show the six digits, zeros included (Section 2.3.5.3).
// RequestPasskey: ask the user for the passkey.  ConfirmNumericValue:
// show the value and ask whether it matches (Section 2.3.5.6.2).
// StartEncryption: run the encryption procedure on the link with
// `ltk`, `ediv` and `rand` (the LE Start Encryption command, [Vol 4]
// Part E, Section 7.8.24); it answers nothing over the air, so the
// procedure continues when the Controller reports the Encryption Change
// event.  PairingComplete: key distribution is over; store
// `result.bond` when `result.bonded`.  PairingFailed: the pairing
// stopped with `reason`, sent by the peer when `by_peer`.  PairingTimeout:
// the Security Manager Timer reached 30 seconds (Section 3.4).
// SecurityEstablished: a bond's LTK encrypted the link, at LE security
// mode 1 `level`.  LocalOobData: the r and C to send to the peer out of
// band.
pub enum SmpInitAction
    DisplayPasskey(passkey: Int)
    RequestPasskey
    ConfirmNumericValue(value: Int)
    StartEncryption(ltk: [u8], ediv: Int, rand: [u8])
    PairingComplete(result: smp_core.PairingResult)
    PairingFailed(reason: Int, by_peer: Bool)
    PairingTimeout
    SecurityEstablished(level: Int)
    // The encryption started with a bond's LTK was refused by the peer:
    // the bond is lost and the peer's identity names it.
    BondLost(peer_address_type: Int, peer_address: [u8])
    LocalOobData(r: [u8], c: [u8])

// ── State ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// The state of both halves is smp_core.PairingState: the fields from
// `phase` down to `peer_csrk` belong to one pairing and are cleared when
// it ends; the random number generator and the key pair outlive
// connections.  `check_sent` records that Ea went out, so a later DHKey
// or user answer does not send a second one.
alias SmpInitState = smp_core.PairingState

// One handler result: the new state, the SMP commands to send in order,
// and at most one action.
struct SmpInitStep
    state: SmpInitState
    pdus: [[u8]]
    action: ?SmpInitAction

// The configuration of a device that has not been configured yet: the
// defaults of smp_responder.nv, which describe the device's IO
// Capability, Bondable mode and key sizes and are the same whichever half
// of a pairing reads them.
pub fn default_config() -> SmpConfig
    smp_core.default_config()

// An initiator with `config`, the local key pair, and a random number
// generator seeded with 16 octets of `seed`.
pub fn new_state(config: SmpConfig, key_pair: KeyPair, seed: [u8]) -> SmpInitState
    smp_core.new_pairing_state(Role.Initiator, config, key_pair, seed)

// A copy of `s` with an empty outbox, which a handler then changes.
fn copy(s: SmpInitState) -> SmpInitState
    smp_core.copy(s)

// ── Queries ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// The peer public key whose DHKey the procedure is waiting for.
pub fn dhkey_request(s: SmpInitState) -> ?PublicKey
    smp_core.dhkey_request(s)

// True while a pairing is in progress on this connection.
fn is_pairing(s: SmpInitState) -> Bool
    smp_core.is_pairing(s)

// The LE security mode 1 level of the pairing in progress.
pub fn pairing_level(s: SmpInitState) -> Int
    smp_core.pairing_level(s)

// True when the private key should be replaced: [Vol 3] Part H,
// Section 2.3.6 recommends a new key pair when S + 3F > 8, S successful
// and F failed pairings since the key was last changed.
fn needs_new_key_pair(s: SmpInitState) -> Bool
    smp_core.needs_new_key_pair(s)

// The key the encryption procedure uses, EDIV and Rand included: the
// bond's ring for a peer that is already bonded.
fn bond_encryption(b: SmpBond) -> SmpInitAction
    StartEncryption(b.ltk, b.ediv, b.rand)

// ── Small helpers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

fn finish(s: SmpInitState, action: ?SmpInitAction) -> SmpInitStep
    SmpInitStep { state: s, pdus: s.outbox, action: action }

// Pairing Failed with `reason`, and the pairing ends.
fn fail(var s: SmpInitState, reason: Reason) -> SmpInitStep
    smp_core.abort(var s, reason, false)
    finish(s, Some(PairingFailed(smp.reason_code(reason), false)))

// A Pairing Failed answer to a command outside a pairing.
fn refuse(var s: SmpInitState, reason: Reason) -> SmpInitStep
    smp_core.decline(var s, reason)
    finish(s, None)

// A Pairing Failed answer to a command the procedure does not expect:
// refused outside a pairing, a failure of the pairing inside one.
fn reject(var s: SmpInitState, reason: Reason) -> SmpInitStep
    if s.phase == Phase.Idle
        refuse(var s, reason)
    else
        fail(s, reason)

// ── The Pairing Feature Exchange ([Vol 3] Part H, Sections 2.3.5.1,
//    3.5.1, 3.5.2) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

// The keys this device offers to distribute: EncKey in LE legacy
// pairing, IdKey when it has an Identity Resolving Key and an Identity
// Address to send with it, SignKey when it signs (Section 3.6.1).
fn offered_init_dist(s: SmpInitState, sc: Bool) -> Int
    var d = 0
    if not sc
        d = d | smp.SMP_KEY_DIST_ENC
    if list.len(s.config.identity_irk) == 16 and list.len(s.config.identity_address) == 6
        d = d | smp.SMP_KEY_DIST_ID
    if s.config.distribute_csrk
        d = d | smp.SMP_KEY_DIST_SIGN
    d

// The keys this device asks the responder for; the responder answers
// with the subset of them it holds (Section 3.6.1).
fn offered_resp_dist(sc: Bool) -> Int
    if sc
        smp.SMP_KEY_DIST_ID | smp.SMP_KEY_DIST_SIGN
    else
        smp.SMP_KEY_DIST_ENC | smp.SMP_KEY_DIST_ID | smp.SMP_KEY_DIST_SIGN

// The Out of Band Data Flag of the Pairing Request: set when this device
// holds the peer's out of band data (Section 2.3.5.1).
fn local_oob_flag(s: SmpInitState, sc: Bool) -> Bool
    if sc
        list.len(s.peer_oob_r) == 16 and list.len(s.peer_oob_c) == 16
    else
        list.len(s.legacy_oob_tk) == 16

// Start a pairing at `level`, or encrypt with the bond when the peer is
// already bonded ([Vol 3] Part H, Section 2.4.4.2).
@satisfies("REQ-BLE-SMP-004")
@satisfies("REQ-BLE-SMP-014")
@satisfies("REQ-BLE-SMP-032")
fn start_pairing(var s: SmpInitState, level: Int) -> SmpInitStep
    if s.phase != Phase.Idle or s.timed_out
        return finish(s, None)
    match s.bond
        Some(b) =>
            if list.len(b.ltk) == 16
                s.requested_level = level
                s.encrypting_with_bond = true
                smp_core.start_timer(var s)
                return finish(s, Some(bond_encryption(b)))
        None    => ()
    s.requested_level = level
    let sc = s.config.secure_connections
    let auth = smp_core.local_auth_req(s.config, smp_core.required_level(s))
    let preq = smp.build_pairing_request(
        s.config.io_capability,
        (if local_oob_flag(s, sc) then smp.SMP_OOB_PRESENT else smp.SMP_OOB_NOT_PRESENT),
        auth,
        s.config.max_key_size,
        offered_init_dist(s, sc),
        offered_resp_dist(sc))
    s.preq = preq[:]
    s.pres = []
    s.replaced_bond = s.bond != None
    smp_core.start_timer(var s)
    smp_core.send(var s, preq)
    s.phase = Phase.PairingResponse
    finish(s, None)

// The Pairing Response, and with it the association model
// (Sections 2.3.5.1, 2.3.5.5 and 2.3.5.6).  The model comes from
// select_method with this device's parameters as the initiator's, which
// is the table the responder reads with the two devices the other way
// round.
@satisfies("REQ-BLE-SMP-005")
@satisfies("REQ-BLE-SMP-023")
@satisfies("REQ-BLE-SMP-030")
@satisfies("REQ-BLE-SMP-032")
fn on_pairing_response(var s: SmpInitState, pdu: [u8]) -> SmpInitStep
    if s.phase != Phase.PairingResponse
        return fail(s, Reason.UnspecifiedReason)
    let resp_io = pdu[1] as Int
    let resp_oob = pdu[2] as Int
    let resp_auth = pdu[3] as Int
    let max_key = pdu[4] as Int
    let fault = smp_core.feature_fault(resp_io, resp_oob, max_key)
    if fault != None
        return fail(s, fault!)
    let level = smp_core.required_level(s)
    let req_auth = s.preq[3] as Int
    // LE Secure Connections run when this device asked for them and the
    // responder answered with them; a responder that answers without the
    // SC bit pairs in LE legacy, as the responding half does when a
    // Pairing Request arrives without it.  Only a device that REQUIRES
    // them fails the pairing over the difference (Section 2.3.5.1).
    let sc = s.config.secure_connections and smp_core.has(req_auth, smp.SMP_AUTHREQ_SC) and smp_core.has(resp_auth, smp.SMP_AUTHREQ_SC)
    if smp_core.sc_missing(s, level, sc)
        return fail(s, Reason.AuthenticationRequirements)
    let key_size = smp_core.negotiated_key_size(s, max_key)
    if smp_core.key_size_too_small(s, key_size, level)
        return fail(s, Reason.EncryptionKeySize)
    let method = smp_core.select_method(sc, s.config.io_capability, local_oob_flag(s, sc),
                                            smp_core.has(req_auth, smp.SMP_AUTHREQ_MITM),
                                            resp_io, resp_oob == smp.SMP_OOB_PRESENT,
                                            smp_core.has(resp_auth, smp.SMP_AUTHREQ_MITM))
    if level >= 3 and method == Method.JustWorks
        return fail(s, Reason.AuthenticationRequirements)
    let bonding = smp_core.has(req_auth, smp.SMP_AUTHREQ_BONDING) and smp_core.has(resp_auth, smp.SMP_AUTHREQ_BONDING)
    if sc
        smp_core.renew_key_pair(var s)
    s.pres = pdu[:]
    // The response's Key Distribution fields are the offer answered:
    // field 5 is what this device distributes, field 6 what the
    // responder does (Section 3.6.1).
    // The Peripheral shall not set a flag the Central left at zero
    // (Section 3.6.1), so each field is masked with the offer in the
    // Pairing Request; in LE Secure Connections EncKey is ignored.
    let answered = if sc
        smp.SMP_KEY_DIST_ID | smp.SMP_KEY_DIST_SIGN
    else
        7
    let init_dist = if bonding
        pdu[5] as Int & s.preq[5] as Int & answered
    else
        0
    let resp_dist = if bonding
        pdu[6] as Int & s.preq[6] as Int & answered
    else
        0
    smp_core.settle(var s, sc, method, key_size, bonding,
                    smp_core.has(req_auth, smp.SMP_AUTHREQ_KEYPRESS) and smp_core.has(resp_auth, smp.SMP_AUTHREQ_KEYPRESS),
                    init_dist, resp_dist)
    var action: ?SmpInitAction = None
    if sc
        // The initiator's Pairing Public Key goes first (Figure 2.4).
        smp_core.send(var s, smp.build_pairing_public_key(s.key_pair.public_key.x, s.key_pair.public_key.y))
        s.phase = Phase.PublicKeyExchange
    else
        s.phase = Phase.LegacyConfirm
        s.local_rand = smp_core.draw(var s)
        if method == Method.JustWorks
            s.tk = smp_keys.zeros(16)
        else if method == Method.OutOfBand
            s.tk = s.legacy_oob_tk
        else if method == Method.PasskeyDisplay
            // The responder displays; this device's user types it.
            action = Some(RequestPasskey)
        else
            s.passkey = smp_core.draw_passkey(var s)
            s.tk = smp_keys.passkey_tk(s.passkey)
            action = Some(DisplayPasskey(s.passkey))
        legacy_send_confirm(var s)
    finish(s, action)

// ── LE legacy pairing, the Short Term Key generation ([Vol 3] Part H,
//    Section 2.3.5.5) ────────────────────────────────────────────────

// Whether the TK is known, which is when LP_CONFIRM_I can go out and
// not before: a typed passkey arrives after the Pairing Response.
fn legacy_confirm_possible(s: SmpInitState) -> Bool
    list.len(s.tk) == 16 and list.len(s.local_rand) == 16

// LP_CONFIRM_I, once the TK is known: the initiator sends its confirm
// before the responder sends its own (Figure 2.2).
fn legacy_send_confirm(var s: SmpInitState)
    if legacy_confirm_possible(s)
        smp_core.send(var s, smp.build_pairing_confirm(smp_core.legacy_confirm_value(s, s.local_rand)))
        s.phase = Phase.LegacyConfirm

@satisfies("REQ-BLE-SMP-006")
fn on_legacy_confirm(var s: SmpInitState, pdu: [u8]) -> SmpInitStep
    s.peer_confirm = smp.field_bytes(pdu, 1, 16)
    // LP_RAND_I goes out once LP_CONFIRM_R is in, so both confirms are on
    // the wire before either random is (Section 2.3.5.5).
    smp_core.send(var s, smp.build_pairing_random(s.local_rand))
    s.phase = Phase.LegacyRandom
    finish(s, None)

@satisfies("REQ-BLE-SMP-007")
@satisfies("REQ-BLE-SMP-029")
@satisfies("REQ-BLE-SMP-033")
fn on_legacy_random(var s: SmpInitState, pdu: [u8]) -> SmpInitStep
    let rand_r = smp.field_bytes(pdu, 1, 16)
    // LP_CONFIRM_R equal to the LP_CONFIRM_I this device sent: the
    // responder has echoed the confirm back instead of computing one from
    // a random of its own, which `legacy_peer_random_holds` rejects with
    // Confirm Value Failed.  SM/CEN/JW/BI-06-C and SM/CEN/PKE/BI-03-C have
    // the Lower Tester drive it (its step 4 lets the IUT send LP_RAND_I
    // first, and step 5 waits for the failure).
    if not smp_core.legacy_peer_random_holds(s, rand_r)
        return fail(s, Reason.ConfirmValueFailed)
    s.peer_rand = rand_r[:]
    s.session_key = smp_core.legacy_short_term_key(s, rand_r)
    s.phase = Phase.Encryption
    finish(s, Some(StartEncryption(s.session_key, 0, smp_keys.zeros(8))))

// ── LE Secure Connections, the Long Term Key generation ([Vol 3]
//    Part H, Section 2.3.5.6) ───────────────────────────────────────

// The responder's Pairing Public Key, and with it the first step of the
// association model's authentication stage (Section 2.3.5.6.1).
@satisfies("REQ-BLE-SMP-015")
fn on_public_key(var s: SmpInitState, pdu: [u8]) -> SmpInitStep
    let peer = PublicKey { x: smp.field_bytes(pdu, 1, 32), y: smp.field_bytes(pdu, 33, 32) }
    let fault = smp_core.public_key_fault(s, peer)
    if fault != None
        return fail(s, fault!)
    s.peer_key = peer
    s.dhkey_wanted = true
    var action: ?SmpInitAction = None
    if smp_core.is_passkey_entry(s)
        s.round = 0
        s.phase = Phase.ScConfirm
        if s.method == Method.PasskeyDisplay
            // The responder displays; this device's user types it.
            action = Some(RequestPasskey)
        else
            s.passkey = smp_core.draw_passkey(var s)
            action = Some(DisplayPasskey(s.passkey))
        passkey_send_confirm(var s)
    else if s.method == Method.OutOfBand
        // Step 4 of Figure 2.5, the Out of Band model's own check: Cb =
        // f4(PKbx, PKbx, rb, 0) over the public key the responder just
        // sent, against the C it published out of band.  It is this
        // moment -- PKbx is in, Na is not out yet -- that the model
        // compares them, and a mismatch ends the pairing here with
        // Confirm Value Failed (Section 2.3.5.6.4, and SM/CEN/SCOB/
        // BI-04-C's step 3, whose Lower Tester sends the wrong C and
        // waits for the Pairing Failed).
        if local_oob_flag(s, true) and not smp_core.oob_confirm_matches(s, peer.x)
            return fail(s, Reason.ConfirmValueFailed)
        s.local_rand = smp_core.draw(var s)
        smp_core.send(var s, smp.build_pairing_random(s.local_rand))
        s.phase = Phase.ScRandom
    else
        // Just Works and Numeric Comparison: Na goes out once the
        // responder's Cb is in, and there is no Ca.
        s.phase = Phase.ScConfirm
    finish(s, action)

// Cai = f4(PKax, PKbx, Nai, Zi), once the passkey and the round's Na are
// known (Section 2.3.5.6.3).
fn passkey_send_confirm(var s: SmpInitState)
    if s.passkey >= 0 and s.phase == Phase.ScConfirm and list.len(s.peer_confirm) == 0
        smp_core.send(var s, smp.build_pairing_confirm(smp_core.passkey_round_confirm(var s)))

// Cb, in Passkey Entry the round's Cbi and otherwise the one the
// responder sent with its public key.
fn on_sc_confirm(var s: SmpInitState, pdu: [u8]) -> SmpInitStep
    s.peer_confirm = smp.field_bytes(pdu, 1, 16)
    if smp_core.is_passkey_entry(s)
        if list.len(s.local_rand) != 16
            return finish(s, None)
    else
        s.local_rand = smp_core.draw(var s)
    smp_core.send(var s, smp.build_pairing_random(s.local_rand))
    s.phase = Phase.ScRandom
    finish(s, None)

fn on_sc_random(var s: SmpInitState, pdu: [u8]) -> SmpInitStep
    let nb = smp.field_bytes(pdu, 1, 16)
    s.peer_rand = nb[:]
    var action: ?SmpInitAction = None
    if smp_core.is_passkey_entry(s)
        if not smp_core.passkey_round_holds(s, nb)
            return fail(s, Reason.ConfirmValueFailed)
        s.round = s.round + 1
        s.peer_confirm = []
        if s.round < smp_core.PASSKEY_ROUNDS
            // The next round's Cai goes out at once (Section 2.3.5.6.3).
            s.local_rand = []
            s.phase = Phase.ScConfirm
            passkey_send_confirm(var s)
        else
            // The twentieth round's Nai and Nbi STAY.  They are the Na and
            // Nb Authentication stage 2 takes: Section 2.3.5.6.3 pairs the
            // last round's nonces with the f5 and f6 values that follow it,
            // and the rig found the failure of a dropped one -- f5 over an
            // empty nonce, and a Lower Tester answering DHKey Check Failed.
            s.phase = Phase.DhKeyCheck
    else
        if s.method == Method.OutOfBand
            // The Out of band model's Cb check again, for the case where
            // the pair was handed to this half after the peer's public key
            // was in: the public key handler above is where the model runs
            // it (Section 2.3.5.6.4), and the same check here catches the
            // data that arrived too late for that step.
            if local_oob_flag(s, true) and not smp_core.oob_confirm_matches(s, s.peer_key.x)
                return fail(s, Reason.ConfirmValueFailed)
        else if not smp_keys.equal_ct(smp_keys.sc_confirm(s.peer_key.x, smp_core.local_x(s), nb, 0), s.peer_confirm)
            return fail(s, Reason.ConfirmValueFailed)
        s.phase = Phase.DhKeyCheck
        if s.method == Method.NumericComparison
            action = Some(ConfirmNumericValue(smp_core.numeric_comparison_value(s)))
    try_e_check(var s)
    finish(s, action)

// Authentication stage 2 (Section 2.3.5.6.5): once the DHKey and, in
// Numeric Comparison, the user's confirmation are in, send Ea.  Answers
// None while something is missing or Ea is already out.
@satisfies("REQ-BLE-SMP-016")
@satisfies("REQ-BLE-SMP-027")
fn try_e_check(var s: SmpInitState) -> ?SmpInitStep
    if s.phase != Phase.DhKeyCheck or list.len(s.dhkey) != 32 or s.check_sent
        return None
    if s.method == Method.NumericComparison and not s.numeric_confirmed
        return None
    let keys = smp_core.sc_keys_of(s)
    smp_core.send(var s, smp.build_pairing_dhkey_check(smp_core.dhkey_check_a(s, keys)))
    s.check_sent = true
    Some(finish(s, None))

// Eb, the responder's DHKey Check: check it against the MacKey and the
// LTK of f5, and start the encryption procedure with that LTK
// (Sections 2.2.7 and 2.4.4.1).
@satisfies("REQ-BLE-SMP-026")
@satisfies("REQ-BLE-SMP-033")
fn on_dhkey_check(var s: SmpInitState, pdu: [u8]) -> SmpInitStep
    if s.phase != Phase.DhKeyCheck or not s.check_sent or list.len(s.dhkey) != 32
        return fail(s, Reason.UnspecifiedReason)
    let keys = smp_core.sc_keys_of(s)
    if not smp_keys.equal_ct(smp_core.dhkey_check_b(s, keys), smp.field_bytes(pdu, 1, 16))
        return fail(s, Reason.DhKeyCheckFailed)
    s.session_key = smp_keys.mask_key(keys.ltk, s.key_size)
    s.phase = Phase.Encryption
    finish(s, Some(StartEncryption(s.session_key, 0, smp_keys.zeros(8))))

fn send_e_check_or_wait(var s: SmpInitState) -> SmpInitStep
    let sent = try_e_check(var s)
    if sent != None
        return sent!
    finish(s, None)

// ── Transport Specific Key Distribution ([Vol 3] Part H, Section 3.6)

// Send the initiator's keys in the order of Section 3.6.1, then wait for
// the responder's or complete.
fn start_key_distribution(var s: SmpInitState) -> SmpInitStep
    smp_core.send_local_keys(var s)
    s.phase = Phase.KeyDistribution
    smp_core.expect_distribution(var s)
    next_expected(var s)

// Expect the next key of the responder, or complete the pairing.
fn next_expected(var s: SmpInitState) -> SmpInitStep
    if smp_core.expect_next_key(var s)
        return finish(s, None)
    complete(s)

fn on_distributed_key(var s: SmpInitState, pdu: [u8]) -> SmpInitStep
    match smp_core.take_distributed_key(var s, pdu)
        Rejected(reason) => fail(s, reason)
        Waiting          => finish(s, None)
        Complete         => complete(s)

fn complete(var s: SmpInitState) -> SmpInitStep
    let result = smp_core.conclude(var s)
    finish(s, Some(PairingComplete(result)))

// ── Received commands ───────────────────────────────────────────────

fn on_pdu(var s: SmpInitState, pdu: [u8]) -> SmpInitStep
    match smp_core.classify(var s, pdu)
        Ignore             => finish(s, None)
        PeerFailed(reason) => finish(s, Some(PairingFailed(reason, true)))
        Refuse(reason)     => refuse(var s, reason)
        Fail(reason)       => fail(s, reason)
        Handle(command)    => on_command(var s, command, pdu)

fn on_command(var s: SmpInitState, command: Command, pdu: [u8]) -> SmpInitStep
    if command == Command.SecurityRequest
        // The Peripheral asks for security (Section 3.6.7): the pairing
        // starts at the level its AuthReq asks for, and a request that
        // arrives while a pairing runs is ignored.
        if s.phase != Phase.Idle
            return finish(s, None)
        let auth = pdu[1] as Int
        let level = if smp.auth_req_mitm(auth)
            3
        else
            2
        return start_pairing(var s, level)
    if command == Command.PairingRequest
        // Only the initiating device sends one (Section 3.5.1).
        return reject(s, Reason.CommandNotSupported)
    let p = s.phase
    if p == Phase.PairingResponse and command == Command.PairingResponse
        return on_pairing_response(var s, pdu)
    // LP_CONFIRM_R counts only after LP_CONFIRM_I has gone out (Figure
    // 2.2): taking it earlier would send LP_RAND_I with no confirm
    // before it, and a peer holding both could search the passkey.
    if p == Phase.LegacyConfirm and command == Command.PairingConfirm and list.len(s.peer_confirm) == 0 and legacy_confirm_possible(s)
        return on_legacy_confirm(var s, pdu)
    if p == Phase.LegacyRandom and command == Command.PairingRandom
        return on_legacy_random(var s, pdu)
    if p == Phase.PublicKeyExchange and command == Command.PairingPublicKey
        return on_public_key(var s, pdu)
    if p == Phase.ScConfirm and command == Command.PairingConfirm and list.len(s.peer_confirm) == 0
        return on_sc_confirm(var s, pdu)
    if p == Phase.ScRandom and command == Command.PairingRandom
        return on_sc_random(var s, pdu)
    if p == Phase.DhKeyCheck and command == Command.PairingDhKeyCheck and s.check_sent
        return on_dhkey_check(var s, pdu)
    if p == Phase.KeyDistribution or p == Phase.Encryption and s.expecting
        return on_distributed_key(var s, pdu)
    reject(s, Reason.UnspecifiedReason)

// ── Encryption ([Vol 3] Part H, Sections 2.4.4, 2.4.4.1, 2.4.4.2) ───

@satisfies("REQ-BLE-SMP-033")
fn on_encryption_changed(var s: SmpInitState, enabled: Bool) -> SmpInitStep
    if s.phase == Phase.Encryption
        if enabled
            return start_key_distribution(var s)
        return fail(s, Reason.UnspecifiedReason)
    if s.phase == Phase.Idle and s.encrypting_with_bond
        s.encrypting_with_bond = false
        if enabled
            return finish(s, Some(SecurityEstablished(smp_core.bond_encryption_established(var s))))
        // The peer refused the encryption started with the bond's LTK --
        // the Controller reports it as PIN or Key Missing -- so the
        // bond is lost: this end keeps it no longer, and the peer is
        // told with the Bond Lost event.  A later pairing with the
        // device therefore starts from a Pairing Request and not from
        // another encryption attempt with a key the peer no longer has
        // (GAP/SEC/SEM/BV-45-C is the case that measures it: its Lower
        // Tester fails the encryption and the IUT pairs again).
        s.timer_deadline = -1
        s.requested_level = 0
        let lost = s.bond!
        s.bond = None
        return finish(s, Some(BondLost(lost.peer_address_type, lost.peer_address[:])))
    finish(s, None)

// ── User and program inputs ─────────────────────────────────────────

// A passkey typed before the Pairing Public Key exchange (or before the
// Pairing Response of LE legacy pairing) is kept until the first round
// needs it.
fn on_passkey(var s: SmpInitState, passkey: Int) -> SmpInitStep
    match smp_core.take_passkey(var s, passkey)
        Ignored         => finish(s, None)
        Refused(reason) => fail(s, reason)
        Accepted        =>
            if s.sc
                passkey_send_confirm(var s)
            else
                legacy_send_confirm(var s)
            finish(s, None)

fn on_numeric(var s: SmpInitState, accepted: Bool) -> SmpInitStep
    match smp_core.take_numeric(var s, accepted)
        Ignored         => finish(s, None)
        Refused(reason) => fail(s, reason)
        Accepted        => send_e_check_or_wait(var s)

fn on_dhkey(var s: SmpInitState, dhkey: [u8]) -> SmpInitStep
    match smp_core.take_dhkey(var s, dhkey)
        Ignored         => finish(s, None)
        Refused(reason) => fail(s, reason)
        Accepted        => send_e_check_or_wait(var s)

fn on_keypress(var s: SmpInitState, notification_type: Int) -> SmpInitStep
    smp_core.send_keypress(var s, notification_type)
    finish(s, None)

fn on_create_oob(var s: SmpInitState) -> SmpInitStep
    let c = smp_core.create_oob_confirm(var s)
    finish(s, Some(LocalOobData(s.local_oob_r, c)))

fn on_tick(var s: SmpInitState) -> SmpInitStep
    if smp_core.timer_due(s)
        smp_core.expire(var s)
        return finish(s, Some(PairingTimeout))
    finish(s, None)

// ── The handler ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

fn is_link_event(input: SmpInitInput) -> Bool
    match input
        Connected(_, _, _, _, _) => true
        Disconnected             => true
        _                        => false

// Advance the procedure by one input at time `now_ms`.
pub fn handle(state: SmpInitState, input: SmpInitInput, now_ms: Int) -> SmpInitStep
    var s = copy(state)
    s.now = now_ms
    // The timer runs out before any later input of the connection is
    // looked at.
    if s.timer_deadline >= 0 and now_ms >= s.timer_deadline and not is_link_event(input)
        return on_tick(var s)
    match input
        Connected(own_type, own_address, peer_type, peer_address, bond) =>
            smp_core.link_up(var s, own_type, own_address, peer_type, peer_address, bond)
            finish(s, None)
        Disconnected                                                    =>
            if smp_core.link_down(var s)
                return finish(s, Some(PairingFailed(smp.reason_code(Reason.UnspecifiedReason), false)))
            finish(s, None)
        Pdu(pdu)                                                        => on_pdu(s, pdu)
        StartPairing(level)                                             => start_pairing(var s, level)
        Tick                                                            => on_tick(var s)
        EncryptionChanged(enabled)                                      => on_encryption_changed(var s, enabled)
        PasskeyEntered(passkey)                                         => on_passkey(var s, passkey)
        NumericConfirmed(accepted)                                      => on_numeric(var s, accepted)
        DhKeyComputed(dhkey)                                            => on_dhkey(var s, dhkey)
        SendKeypress(t)                                                 => on_keypress(var s, t)
        SetLegacyOobTk(tk)                                              =>
            smp_core.set_legacy_oob_tk(var s, tk)
            finish(s, None)
        SetPeerOobData(r, c)                                            =>
            smp_core.set_peer_oob_data(var s, r, c)
            finish(s, None)
        CreateOobData                                                   => on_create_oob(var s)
        SetLocalOobData(r)                                              =>
            smp_core.set_local_oob_data(var s, r)
            finish(s, None)
        Reseed(seed)                                                    =>
            smp_core.reseed(var s, seed)
            finish(s, None)
        Cancel                                                          =>
            if s.phase == Phase.Idle
                return finish(s, None)
            fail(s, Reason.UnspecifiedReason)

// ── Fixtures that the suites of other modules share ─────────────────────
//
// The tests play the responder against this device with the same toolbox
// functions the responder's own tests use, and one of them runs the two
// halves against each other, which is the interop check the two modules'
// own tests cannot make: every value this module sends is accepted by
// smp_responder.nv and every value it accepts is one the responder sends.
//
// A test that pairs in LE legacy mode uses `config_legacy`, a device
// whose Pairing Request carries no SC bit: a device that asks for LE
// Secure Connections and is answered without them fails the pairing
// (Section 2.3.5.1), which `test_the_sc_bit_must_be_answered` checks.
// The peer's key pair is `responder_key_pair`, not the debug key pair
// the responder's own tests use for their peer, because this device
// refuses a debug public key while `accept_debug_key` is clear.

fn hex(text: Str) -> [u8]
    bytes.to_byte_list(bytes.from_hex(text)!)

fn own_address() -> [u8]
    hex("c5c4c3c2c1c0")

fn peer_address() -> [u8]
    hex("a5a4a3a2a1a0")

fn seed() -> [u8]
    hex("0f0e0d0c0b0a09080706050403020100")
